/*
   Description
   -----------
  Take data from ADC for I and Q channels, selection of I and Q channels done
  though usage of the logical addresses of PSEL. 
     if pdx0 -> I channel selected, no latch of the data (transparent mode)
     if pdx1 -> Q channel selected, no latch of the data (transparent mode)
     if pdx4 -> I channel selected, data is latched
     if pdx5 -> Q channel selected, data is latched
  For best operation
   1. alternate pdx4 for I channel with pdx1 for Q channel
   2. or alternate pdx0 with pdx1 each sample
   3. or alternate pdx0 with pdx1 each turn.

  For this function the first options are selected.

  First four samples are taken in order to synchronise PIDS and data latch
  strobe. Also 1 clock latency has to be taken  in to  account when numbers of
  read are counted 
	Registers:
	---------
		r3 - pointer to I channel
		r2 - pointer to Q channel
	Due to latency I data are read to r2 but actually they are transfered
	on the next cycle or to r3.
	Due to latency Q data are read to r3 but actually they are transfered
	on the next cycle or to r2. 

		r2 = Q_DAT_BUF
		r3 = I_DAT_BUF
*/

 	*r2 = pdx4
	*r3 = pdx1
 	*r2 = pdx4
	*r3 = pdx1		/* four initial samples */
 	*r2++ = pdx4		/* start to take 288 samples - 144 for I and */
